For the most extravagant women of fashion designers offer "predatory" drawings, but even the classic leopard or snake print this season is made in pastel and very gentle tones and absolutely devoid of aggressiveness. Sexuality of such drawings in this season beautifully shades all shades of blue, mint and ecru.
It is difficult to choose exactly the model that will decorate the figure and emphasize its individuality. To do this, you need to accurately answer the question: what swimsuits are in the 2018 fashion?
In the trend this summer, knitted models returned - as an echo of a very fashionable "linen" style. This trend is most accurately embodied monokini with wide openwork slats, reminiscent of handmade lace.
Preference is given to large textile brooches-flowers, ruffles, flounces and effectively tied straps. The accent in the decor of most collections is made on spectacular accessories - bracelets, necklaces, hats, sunglasses, supporting style, color scheme and the image created by the swimsuit in general.
A study by the University of Manchester showed that the lack of proper screening for gestational diabetes increases the number of stillbirths. The results of the study were published in the English language journal BJOG.
The British study involved pregnant women from the 41 maternity hospital. It was found that not all women at high risk for gestational diabetes were examined as needed.
Without treatment, the condition can significantly increase the risk of complications.
Researchers suggest that women at risk should be evaluated regularly after 26 weeks. A secondary mandatory test should be performed later during pregnancy.
Any woman can develop gestational diabetes during pregnancy. The risk is significantly increased if the body mass index (BMI) exceeds 30 or the woman had diabetes mellitus before.
In Russia, a glucose tolerance test is offered at 24 – 27 week of pregnancy. Affected women undergo a preliminary test, and then the main one.
Exercise also helps to normalize glucose in the bloodstream. Some pregnant women have constantly high sugar levels, so it is recommended that you inject with insulin.
If there are signs of diabetes mellitus - increased thirst, headache and fatigue - it is recommended to visit a doctor immediately. Timely therapy significantly prevents complications.
