До Inventions antibiotics, mortality was extremely high, every third person died from pneumonia. To date, the situation has changed, properly selected treatment allows to avoid complications, leads to complete recovery.
When bacteria get into the respiratory tract, the cells of the immune system neutralize it, thereby preventing inflammation. If the immunity is weakened, the microbes freely penetrate into the lungs, which leads to pneumonia.
• Occupational hazards (dust, work in mines, in chemical plants without adequate protection).
Manifestations of pneumonia are diverse, they depend on the aggressiveness of the pathogen, the state of the human immune system, and age. In some cases, the first signs of pneumonia in adults are easy to overlook or confuse with banal ARI, as the clinical picture can be erased.
For further diagnosis and treatment of pneumonia in adults, the color of sputum, separated by coughing, is important. Yellow, green color indicates a bacterial nature, transparent or white - more characteristic of viral damage to the lungs.
• Sweating, rapid pulse are additional symptoms of pneumonia in adults.
• Chest pain is most often associated with cough, suggesting pleural involvement in the process of inflammation.
• Hemoptysis is an adverse sign of pneumonia in adults. Blood in the sputum appears due to the rupture of small vessels with a strong dry cough, and is also a symptom of more serious diseases: tuberculosis, lung cancer.
Sometimes pneumonia has an erased flow - without raising the temperature. Only weakness, loss of appetite, rapid breathing, periodic cough draws attention.
Diagnosis with a typical course of the disease for an experienced doctor is not difficult. It is much harder to suspect pneumonia, when there are no main signs: fever, cough, chest pain.
• In the biochemical analysis of blood for pneumonia, acute phase proteins are determined. Also important are renal and hepatic parameters (creatinine, urea, AST, ALT).
• Bacterioscopy, sputum bakposev with the determination of antibiotic sensitivity. The phlegm is collected before starting antibiotics This analysis allows you to identify the causative agent of pneumonia, as well as the drug that will be most effective in a particular case.
It is very important not to engage in self-medication, even with slightly expressed symptoms, this can lead to a prolonged course, serious complications.
• During the entire period of illness the patient must observe bed rest.
The medical treatment of bacterial pneumonia in adults begins with the choice of an antibiotic. The doctor prescribes the drug right away, without waiting for the results of bakposseva.
Primary prevention is aimed at preventing the development of the disease. If you follow simple rules, you can avoid the occurrence of pneumonia.
