The meaning of the name Emma
The meaning of Emma's name, variants of origin and history. What awaits a girl named Emma: what is the nature and fate of its possessor
In Russia, girls with the name Emma you meet infrequently. Nevertheless, there are parents who choose it for their daughters, predetermining the nature and fate of Emma.
The origin and history of the name Emma is ambiguous. There are not one or two, but five versions of his education.
German version - the most understandable, since the name is really common in German-speaking countries. It has one root with the German word "ermen", which means "universal", "whole", and, in the opinion of scientists, can be its short form.
5. The ancient Greek version gives the following interpretation: “flattering”, “affectionate”.
Arabic version also is. The translation sounds like "reliable", "calm", "true".
Emma avoids noisy parties, preferring to spend time with a book in her hands. She is faithful, noble, honest, will never reveal another's secret, but she will not trust anyone either.
The fate of a woman named Emma
She can get on with almost any person, but she prefers a man of experience and strength. Possessing the developed intuition and gift of the psychologist, she feels the slightest mood of the spouse and is able to deftly avoid acute situations.
