Someone buys extremely expensive branded delicacies, while others are happy to share sweets and sausages from the table. Opinions vary, but what is the truth?
Goodies are supplements to the diet. Besides the fact that goodies bring joy to dogs and cats, when properly served, they are also very useful.
Such a diet is harmful, and with regular eating is quite dangerous for the health of the pet. In order not to risk the well-being of the pet, certain foods must be completely excluded from the diet.
sweets (upset metabolism, provoke diseases of the digestive system, problems with teeth);
seasoned, savory goodies (disrupt metabolism, provoke fluid retention in the body, often can cause gastritis);
Even a small portion of dry food in the form of a treat is sometimes enough to provoke at least discomfort in the pet. And with regular such violations of the diet over time, numerous diseases arise that are not always treatable.
Caution should be taken with milk and dairy products. These are useful products, but not everyone can assimilate them.
For older pets, you almost always have to remove milk from the list of products, as over time the body ceases to produce an enzyme that is involved in its processing.
To please a dog or a cat, you can buy at the pet store or veterinary pharmacy any suitable breed, age and size of a four-legged friend's goodies. You can even find dogs approved for use in dogs that are sugar and caffeine free.
In addition to branded products, you can treat your pet with other pleasant and useful products:
cartilage (raw, boiled or dried in the oven);
Moderation also plays an important role. You can’t feed your pet with even the most healthy goodies.
Secondly, excessive encouragement adversely affects the behavior of a four-legged friend. A pet can either get used to eating the most delicious and refuse any other food in the future, or it can simply get tired of the monotony.
It should be remembered that goodies are an important addition to the diet of cats and dogs.
