Almost always during a mandatory monthly check-up in an out-patient department, someone from pediatricians (pediatrician, neurologist, orthopedist) advises parents to write a child for a course of health massage.
It is only necessary to understand some of the nuances of this procedure.
In the first year of life, it is very important to closely monitor the child and his development. There are some points that are indicative of the need to contact the local pediatrician and neurologist as soon as possible to prescribe a course of therapeutic massage:
• At the age of 4-5 months, the child does not attempt to turn from the back to the abdomen and back;
• At the age of 7-7,5 months the child does not know how to sit confidently without support, strongly bends the backrest with an arch, collapses on its side;
• At the age of 9 months, he does not attempt to stand up independently and stand by the support;
These symptoms are most often associated with a violation of muscle tone, as a result of which the child is physically unable to acquire the necessary skills in time. Already after the first course of massage, everything starts to come back to normal and the child develops further by age.
Despite the fact that massage is very useful for a child at any age, there are some categories that massage is strictly contraindicated!
• People with acute respiratory infections, especially if accompanied by high fever (above 37,5);
• having poor blood coagulation and prone to bleeding;
If the child does not have any special indications or contraindications, you can ask the pediatrician to tell and show how to properly massage the newborn, so as not only to not harm the baby, but also to benefit. Or, independently, find information and training photos and videos on the Internet.
The child should not be hungry, but at the same time the massage can not be done immediately after feeding. Between meals and massage should take at least one hour.
Before the massage, the mother must wash her hands and warm them up, so as not to frighten the child with cold touches.
Ideally, this is a changing table. To the child was more comfortable on it, under the back you can put a few soft diapers or a blanket and a disposable diaper in case the child pee during the massage.
So, the massage of the newborn consists of several complexes, which go in a clear sequence one by one: stroking, rubbing and vibration, gymnastics. Each of these parts should be considered separately to understand their need and fully understand how to properly massage a newborn baby.
It starts with them and each massage ends. Light stroking calms the nervous system, improves blood circulation, warms up the muscles and prepares the tender skin for massage.
The second stage: rubbing, kneading and vibration
Rubbing helps to reduce the increased muscle tone, improve blood circulation in the muscles and, consequently, improve their nutrition, strengthen the tendons and ligaments of the child. The essence of vibration lies in a slight shaking and shaking the child's hands and feet.
The first thing you need to remember - during bloating is unacceptably strong pressure, otherwise you can only aggravate the situation, causing the child painful sensations. The tummy massage itself is performed using four fingers of the hand (without the thumb) in a circular motion clockwise, as this is the way the large intestine in the body is located.
Similar actions occur during the gymnastics of the child's handles: flexion, extension and rotation of the hands, elbows and shoulder joints alternately, raising the handles to the sides and crossing them on the chest.
To finish the massage of the newborn must necessarily stroking to calm his nervous system and relax. Only now it is necessary to act in the reverse order, starting from the head and ending with the legs.
After the parents were convinced of the undoubted benefits of the massage, a completely logical question arises: how often to massage the newborn?
All movements during the massage are carried out along the joints: from the periphery to the center.
During the massage is very important psychological contact with the child: you need to talk with him, sing songs, smile. That's why only my mother knows how to do so that her newborn baby likes the massage and brought him only pleasure.
