In East Austin, the top taco spot Discada, Nixta Taqueria and Cuantos Tacos teamed up to give away free breakfast tacos and tacos this week. Anthony Pratto, the co-owner of Discada, is going to drive the truck this week and has already prepared a dish of the same name (beef, pork and vegetables cooked in layers with a plough pan) over the weekend.
Pratto mixes with 15 eggs in his hand; Nixta’s co-owner and chef Edgar Rico shares a kiosk kitchen with Pratto, He cooked duck and dried chili as a spare. Pratto said that in addition to tacos, you can also make tacos: “It’s very easy.
