SEPOV is an acronym for “Search Engine Point of View”; it is usually used in the context of search engine optimization (SEO) discussions.
This is because every business needs to be on the internet, to one extent or another.
(this one has a caveat)
Number one: They refuse to tell you their methods.
Because the techniques used for successful SEO are not secret.
If your potential SEO “specialist” tells you that their methods are proprietary, it’s a good bet that they’re doing something that the search engines would frown upon.
At best, what they mean is that they took the Google Adwords class or something of that nature.
At worst, they are simply lying.
Now some may make the argument that it is perfectly reasonable for a business to want a non-disclosure agreement signed, and that it is plausible that this SEO firm has only catered to these businesses.
Otherwise, who would hire them except the unwary?
While highly effective, SEO cannot be done overnight.
If they tell you they can offer you an instant solution, just remember TANSTAAFL (There ain’t no such thing as a free lunch).
Every marketer knows the power of a guarantee.
The only way for an SEO professional to honestly provide a guarantee would require them to know the inner workings of the search engine algorithms.
One possible exception would be an SEO professional or firm that offered a PPC deal.
However, it takes time and must often be outsourced.
