Government Websites for Germany:
– PONS dictionary: Useful for beginning and advanced users.
– Wörterbuch.info: Also best used in German to English searches. Includes thesaurus.
– German grammar explained: Our own pages on all aspects of German grammar.
– Langenberg language translation: One-stop shop for multiple translators that handle words, phrases, text blocks, or entire webpages to or from German.
– Systran Language Translation: Translates text blocks and webpages to or from German.
– Deutsche Wellelanguage courses: Courses for beginning, intermediate & business German learners.
– German for Beginners: Basic online course from About.com
– German practice activities,Level 1&Level 2: Our list of interactive self-grading activities for beginning to intermediate learners along with lots of grammar explanations and cultural information.
– The German Professor: Blog with language information and reviews of websites useful for learners
– LiveMochaandBusuu: Language learning communities, where you can be both the teacher (of your native language or another language you know) and the learner.
Culture & information about German-speaking countries
– The German Way: Excellent overview of many aspects of German, Austrian, and Swiss life, behaviors, and attitudes
– History of German-American relations: Chronological overview plus numerous links, provided by the U.S. Embassy
– German-Americans: More than Bratwurst and Beer: Highlights traces of German-American influences around the U.S.
: Essays, maps, & statistics on Germans in America
– Americans and Germans: Close Encounters of a Crosscultural Kind: an online book of interviews with German Americans
– Campus Germany: : A cultural orientation for those intending to study in Germany
– German Culture & Society: Excellent overviews and current news on contemporary social and cultural issues from the Goethe Institut
– German Missions in the U.S.: Website of the German Embassy in Washington, D.C. A multitude of information on German culture and German-American relations
– Austrian National Tourist Office: –Lots of info about travel and culture
– ArtLexGerman Art: Highlights significant works through the centuries
– Contemporary German bands & music: Our own pages on the contemporary German music scene
– German,Austrian, andSwissradio stations: More lists of German-language streaming radio broadcasts
OnlineTVRecorder: Record and download programming on dozens of channels around the clock. There is a learning curve, but the service is free.
– Film.deandMovie.de: Information about the latest movie hits in German theaters
– The media in Germany: Introduction to the print media in Germany. From the Goethe Institut.
– Austrian Literature Online: 5670 public domain documents, including several Austrian literary works.
– Xlibris: Excellent overview of periods with some information on authors and works as well.
– Another glossary of literary terms: A thorough list from The Literary Encyclopedia.
