Plasma contains a large number of active oxygen ions, high-energy free radicals and other components, it is very easy and bacteria, mold and bacterium, viruses in the protein and nucleic acid material oxidation reaction and denaturation, so that all kinds of microbial death.
After the sterilization experiment, through the electron microscope to observe the role of plasma after the bacterial body and virus particles image, showing a lot of holes, which is generated by the high kinetic energy of the electron and ion breakdown etching effect.
In the process of excitation of hydrogen peroxide to form a plasma, accompanied by part of the ultraviolet ray, this high-energy ultraviolet photon are absorbed by microorganisms or viruses in the protein, resulting in its molecular denaturation and inactivation.
Plasma sterilization works continuously and does not produce ultraviolet light, or ozone, to avoid pollution of the environment.
Long service life. Under normal use, its design life of 15 years, while the UV disinfection machine is about 5 years.
Sterilization nzira Hydrogen peroxide plasma technology
Tembiricha yekubereka ye vertical hydrogen peroxide plasma sterilizer is 50℃±5℃, with low temperature and no humidity, and no damage to sterilized items and instruments.
The sterilizing agent adopts hydrogen peroxide liquid, no toxic residue, no need for drainage or exhaust, and no damage to the operator's body. The air inlet and exhaust port have filters, which can fully absorb the H₂O₂ excluded in the process of vacuum residue discharge, with no pollution to the environment.
The sterilization chamber is made of aluminum, which has advantageous anticorrosive thermal conductivity and makes the temperature of the sterilization chamber more balanced and effective. The low-temperature storage system of hydrogen peroxide ensures that the concentration of hydrogen peroxide is stable and effective, and will not evaporate.
3.Check whether the equipment has obvious damage or other abnormalities.
During the sterilization process of the plasma sterilization machine, the operator must not be far away from the equipment and closely observe the operating conditions of the equipment.
All instruments must comply with the standard practice before being placed in the sterilization chamber.
Hydrogen peroxide is a strong oxidizer and is irritating. Do not open the plastic envelope of the hydrogen peroxide cartridge to prevent burns.
Pay attention to hand hygiene, wash hands under the seven-step hand washing method, and use clean hands to touch sterilized items and sterilized items.
To avoid frequent failures of the low-temperature plasma sterilizer during use, proper maintenance and care must be taken.
Clean the impurities in the filter at the discharge port inside the sterilizer to avoid the impurities from entering the exhaust pipe during the operation of the sterilizer.
Check whether the sterilizer door seal is flat, intact, and free from dislodgement and breakage. Check the touch screen; observe whether there is leakage of steam, water, and other media pipelines and valve parts; observe whether the sterilizer operation indicator is intact; once the above parts are found to have problems, the sterilizer should not be used and be used after maintenance and repair.
Clean the exterior of the low-temperature plasma sterilizer to avoid the accumulation of dust, which will shorten the service life of the air filter. Contact between components and water should be avoided, and water should be dried before powering on.
The safety valve, pressure gauge, and temperature gauge of the sterilizer should be inspected annually, and the inspection results should be recorded and kept. The air filter should also be replaced regularly.
