In the laboratory, the hazards of chemicals to the hands are usually divided into the following three categories.
Although vinyl lab gloves are included in the disposable gloves, they offer limited protection against pathogens and contaminants. Therefore, it is not suggested to use it in laboratory environments.
Nitrile gloves for laboratory use
Science lab gloves, as general personal protective equipment, have good abrasion and cut resistance performance. Their main function is to protect the hands of laboratory personnel effectively when exposed to chemical solvents.
However, not all disposable gloves can be used in the laboratory. They need to meet the following requirements.
In various experiments, the experimenters need to contact different live animals or reagents, such as dissecting mice, culturing a variety of bacterial organisms, mixing the required reagents, etc. In the process of these operations, their hand safety needs to be protected by disposable gloves with superior isolation properties.
If they cannot ensure the sensitivity and dexterity of their hands, it will affect the efficiency of the experiment and even lead to large errors in the experimental results. When choosing lab hand gloves, you need to choose disposable gloves that are better fitting, thinner, and more comfortable.
It is not easy to grip glassware and most experimental equipment for their smooth surfaces. Gloves with a good grip can prevent instruments from slipping off and causing unnecessary damage or injury to personnel.
