Types of vacuum pump The types of vacuum pump can be broadly divided into three categories:
Positive displacement pump is a vacuum pump that uses periodic changes in the volume of the pump chamber to complete the suction and discharge process, where the gas is compressed before being discharged. Positive displacement pump is divided into two types which are rotary vane vacuum pump and reciprocating vacuum pump.
It uses the rotating motion of the piston in the pump chamber to suck, compress and discharge the gas. Rotary vacuum pumps are also available in the following forms.
Entrapment pump is a vacuum pump in which gas molecules are adsorbed or condensed on the inner surface of the pump, thus reducing the number of gas molecules in the container and achieving the purpose of pumping. Entrapment pumps are also available in the following forms.
Rotary vane vacuum pump equipped with special design air ballast valve to prevent the pump oil from mixing with water, extending the use time of the pump oil.
Liquid ring vacuum pump is directly connected with the same shaft, which saves space and is easy to install.
High-quality mechanical seal as standard configuration, no leakage, maintenance-free.
Scroll vacuum pump is the impeller for the outer edge of the part with many small vanes of the whole disk, the liquid in the vane and pump body flow channel repeatedly do vortex movement of the pump. Although the vortex pump belongs to the category of vane-type machinery, its working process, structure, and the shape of the characteristic curve and centrifugal pumps and other types of pumps are not quite the same.
