As one of the most important auxiliary equipment in labs, laboratory mixer can be used in many fields. It is suitable for the chemical industry, light industry, pharmaceuticals, and building industries for multi-component solid-solid liquid, solid-liquid, liquid-liquid phase materials mixing, reaction, dispersion, dissolution, hardening, and tempering, and other processes.
When a laboratory mixer is in operation its internal mixing paddles are driven by the power unit and rotate in a fixed direction, the material is used to do axial rotation and radial rotation in the process of rotation. And the material in the lab mixer is also in an axial and circular motion so that the material can be effectively dispersed and stirred in the form of shear and diffusion stirring.
Types of laboratory mixer There are main four types of laboratory mixer which can be used in labs:
Artificial mixer is generally possible with the help of a glass rod, it is a traditional stirring method that can be used to stir to accelerate the dissolution of solutes, and promote mutual dissolution. Glass rod is suitable for simple experiment items, and it is most common in middle school experiment.
