Peristaltic pump is a fluid transfer device that can control the flow rate. Commonly, the fluid in the hose is moved in a specific direction by repeatedly compressing the flexible tube, and the flow rate is determined by the diameter of the tube and the compression speed and used in systems such as liquid phase chromatography and perfusion.
Peristaltic pumps have a wide range of applications, used in the laboratory is called laboratory peristaltic pump, applied in the industrial field is called industrial peristaltic pump, and the pharmaceutical industry will also use peristaltic pump, although the name is different, the core technology is peristaltic pump fluid transfer.
The use of peristaltic pump can easily transport viscous liquids and liquids with fine particles, peristaltic pumps do not need to be cleaned, replace the fluid simply by replacing the hose. Common uses are the dispensing of juice, yogurt, flavorings, syrups, and filling of other food products in the food production line.
Peristaltic pumps can work in continuous fluid transfer situations while identifying and solving many difficult fluid transfer problems peomptly. It can convey sewage, suspended solids, corrosive chemicals, and other difficult fluids, and some of the common uses are fuel liquids, chemical etching fluids for etching, printing inks, laundry chemical solutions, abrasive fluids, lubricating fluids, and other conveyances.
High precision: repeat accuracy, high stability accuracy.
Good sealing: good self-priming ability, can idle, can prevent backflow.
Simple maintenance: no valves and seals.
Compared to pumps with the same rotor diameter, which produce a larger "pillow" volume of the pump, the volume of fluid delivered per rotation of the rotor is also larger, but the degree of pulsation generated is also larger. With the smaller "pillow" volume of the pump, its rotor per revolution of the fluid volume is also smaller; and, the rapid, continuous formation of the small "pillow" so that the fluid flow is smoother.
Hose pump designers and users of the primary value is its ability to transport strong abrasive media. It has no valve, no seal and the only part in contact with the medium is the inner cavity of the rubber hose, the rotor of the compressed hose is completely independent of the medium.
Variable speed peristaltic pump Variable speed peristaltic pump has the basic control functions of peristaltic pump, display speed, start/stop, direction, speed adjustment, filling and emptying, power down memory, external control input, etc.
In addition to the basic functions, flow peristaltic pump adds flow rate display, flow rate calibration, communication, and other functions.
Power Rating 20W
