Dry hot air sterilization is a method to kill microorganisms or eliminate pyrogens by heating the items to be sterilized in dry air to a temperature sufficient to kill bacteria. Dry heat sterilizers have outstanding sterilization efficiency and can kill reproductive bacteria.
The chain control system in the dry heat sterilizer is equipped with door chain control system, pressure sensor, temperature sensor, chain control device for controlling and stopping the operation of the conveyor belt, etc. This can ensure that the sterilized goods are prevented from passing through the sterilizer at a temperature lower than the sterilization temperature when the temperature is lower than the design requirement under any circumstances.
In the dry heat sterilization system, the temperature detection, sensing, control, and recording system is the basis of the whole sterilization process control. The control system must ensure that the sterilization temperature in the chamber of the sterilizer can be maintained within the set sterilization temperature range, and the recording system must record the temperature readings of the temperature detection and sensing system accurately and clearly.
Buffer plates or air stalls are used to control the airflow of the dry heat sterilizer and are mostly installed near the inlet or exhaust air ducts or heaters. Airflow regulators for positive pressure control can be installed near the high-efficiency filters in the exhaust system to prevent backflow air pollution and control the positive pressure by controlling the exhaust air volume, or airflow regulators can be used to control the inlet and exhaust air volumes to maintain positive pressure.
If it is to sterilize glass syringes and other items, the optimum temperature is 170°C and the sterilization time is 1 hour. The methods of dry heat sterilization are dry baking, cauterization or incineration, infrared, microwave and so on.
* Continuous dry heat sterilization equipment, such as tunnel ovens, can be used for the production of small volume injections.
Cooling water consumption 250kg/batch
Equipped with no glass inner door, outer door with observation window.
1. The dry heat sterilizer should not be used under high voltage, high current and strong magnetic field conditions to avoid interference and the risk of electric shock.
Electroplated parts and surface decoration paint should be kept clean frequently, and if they are not used for a long time, neutral grease or petroleum jelly should be applied on the electroplated parts to prevent corrosion.
The shell of the dry heat sterilizer must be effectively grounded, and the power should be turned off after use.
The sterilization box should be placed in a room with good ventilation, and no flammable and explosive items should be placed around it.
