They can cause damage through direct or indirect contact with the hands. For example, if laboratory personnel are often in contact with strong acids or strong bases, their hands will result in skin corrosion and cause severe pain whereas acid mist of hydrofluoric acid will irritate the hands and lead to dermatitis and other symptoms.
Гурав дугаар, low-temperature chemicals frostbite the hands. For example, when having operations with chemicals like liquid nitrogen or dry ice, improper protection is easy to frostbite hands.
The science lab gloves come in different materials such as natural latex rubber, nitrile, neoprene, polyethylene, polychloroprene, PVC, etc. They are made up of using only one material or combination but differ in glove thickness and style.
The neoprene lab gloves are mainly produced from chloroprene emulsion polymerization. They have good resistance to oxidation and hydrocarbon solvent swelling as well as good chemical resistance, physical strength, and aging resistance.
Function of laboratory gloves In the laboratory, the experimenter will inevitably come into contact with a variety of corrosive and other harmful substances when conducting various tests, so the laboratory is a place that requires perfect protection and always needs to wear protective clothing, protective glasses ......
Generally, disposable gloves are used more frequently in the laboratory than reusable gloves for laboratory.
