In the chemical laboratory, the experimental operation produces a variety of harmful gases, odor, moisture, and flammable, explosive, corrosive substances, to protect the safety of users, to prevent the diffusion of pollutants in the experiment to the laboratory, in the vicinity of the pollution source to use laboratory fume hood. Biosafety cabinet
It is widely used in scientific research, teaching, clinical testing, and production in microbiology, genetic engineering, biological products, and other fields. It is the most basic safety protection equipment in experiment.
There is mainly six functions about laboratory fume hood:
Release function Chemical fume hood can absorb harmful gas generated inside the fume hood and let it dilute and exclude outdoor.
Fume hood in a lab has equipped with a non-sliding glass window to separate the inside and outside of the fume hood.
Supplement function When discharging harmful gases, laboratory fume hood can inhale air from outside.
In corrosive experiments using sulfuric acid, nitric acid, hydrofluoric acid, and other strong acid occasions, the overall material of the fume hood is acid and alkali proof, and made of stainless steel or PVC material.
Cabinet Usually made of thick porcelain white PP, the door is made of porcelain white PP, which can be customized according to the different needs of customers, different sizes, the thickness of cabinet, acid and alkaline ability.
* Upper part of cabinet: adopting top exhaust design, and there is an exhaust tuyere of ∮250mm. The guide plate is made of homogeneous PP material with strong acid and alkali resistance.
* Glass of adjusting door: made of transparent tempered glass or organic glass, with excellent acid and alkali resistance.
* Suspension cable of adjusting door: each laboratory fume adjusting door uses a cable to connect.
Lining board 5mm thick high quality pure material PP
Shell 1.0mm cold-rolled steel plate with anti-rust treatment and electrostatic spraying
Window a manual window and can be stopped at any height within the travel range.
Although they are sometimes referred to collectively as "fume hoods," biosafety cabinets and laboratory fume hoods are two entirely different categories of laboratory equipment. Both are built to safely deal with scientific hazards, but they are different in the type of protection they offer, airflow, and application.
* In a Class II biosafety cabinet, intake air is safely pumped around the operator, sterile air flows down to the work surface, and discharged air is filtered by HEPA and then recirculated to the laboratory or released to the atmosphere through a duct system or canopy connection.
At present, spin columns are popular with most laboratories and companies at home and abroad. They use silica membranes as specific adsorbent materials for nucleic acids while remaining largely non-absorbent to other biological materials.
The gasket is a special fiber material that is resistant to acids and bases and most organic solvents and does not adsorb to most biomolecules.
Specially optimized silicone or glass fiber membranes made of imported raw materials can adsorb nucleic acid molecules to the maximum extent.
The inner tube of the reflux condenser is some glass spheres connected for reflux of organic preparations and is suitable for liquids of various boiling points. After long-term use, the rust in the spacer can be washed away with hydrochloric acid.
A ball mill is widely used in the production of cement, silicate products, new construction materials, refractory materials, chemical fertilizers, black and non-ferrous metal beneficiation, and glass-ceramics. It can be used for dry or wet grinding of various ores and other grindable materials.
5) Applied in materials of all degrees of hardness.
The lab rubber mixing mill is composed of a crushing mainframe, motor frame, water cooling, and other systems. Its basic principle is to achieve the purpose of material crushing by shearing and grinding the material through the relative movement of two grinding discs.
The jet mill has the advantages of a wide range of applications and the high fineness of finished products. It can make the machine become inert gas protection equipment by changing the ordinary air in the gas source part to nitrogen, carbon dioxide gas, and other inert gases, which is suitable for the crushing and grading processing of flammable and explosive, easy to oxidize, and other materials.
