Cuvette test tubes are the main instrument used for visual colorimetric analysis in chemical experiments, which can be used to roughly measure the concentration of the solution. When using test tubes for colorimetry, one tube should contain the solution to be measured, while the other cuvette test tube should contain the standard solution.
