What is the principle of biosafety cabinet? හි වැඩ කරන මූලධර්මය biosafety cabinet is mainly to pump the air in the cabinet outward, so that the cabinet maintains negative pressure, through vertical airflow to protect the staff; the outside air in the cabinet also needs to be filtered by HEPA before being discharged into the atmosphere.
The exhaust fan provides the power of exhaust, the unclean air in the working room is extracted and purified by the exhaust filter to protect the sample and the experimental items in the cabinet. Because of the effect of exhaust, the working area is negative pressure to prevent the air escape in the working area, and to protect the operator.
The light source and ultraviolet light source are located inside the glass door to ensure certain brightness of the working room and disinfection of the table and air in the working room.
Operation system The control panel has power supply, ultraviolet lamp, floodlight, fan switch, control front glass door movement and other devices, the main function is to set and display the system state.
According to the NSF49 standard, we can divide biological safety cabinet into three classes to satisfy different demands between biological research and immunization requirements. Biosafety cabinet class 1
Biosafety cabinet class 2 Biosafety cabinet class 2 also has air flow into the front window opening, known as "inlet air flow", to prevent the escape of aerosols that may be generated during microbial operation from the front window.
It is a widely used cabinet type at present. According to the provisions of NSF49, biosafety cabinet class 2 can be divided into 4 types according to the inlet airflow speed, exhaust mode and circulation mode: A1, A2, B1 and B2.
A1 Minimum airflow velocity or average measurement shall be at least 0.38m/s 30% of the gas is filtered out through the exhaust port 70% of the gas is recirculated through the HEPA filter to the work area
