According to our previous definition of laboratory fume hood and biosafety cabinet, we can know that a lab fume hood is a ventilated cabinet that can remove harmful chemical fumes and volatile vapors from the laboratory and provide staff protection only. Biosafety cabinet and utilize HEPA filters to provide environmental, human, and product protection.
වායු දහරාව * Since fume hoods handle hazardous chemicals, air starts at the surface of the equipment, passes through the work surface and is sucked away through the duct system, where it is released into the atmosphere. * Proper and undisturbed air flow in fume hood is essential.
* In a class I biosafety cabinet, air is sucked away and across the work surface by laboratory staff.
* Class III biosafety cabinet is an airtight cabinet with both intake and exhaust filtered by HEPA.
අයදුම්පත Can handle odorous substances, toxic gases, reactive substances, chemicals that may fly, aerosols, carcinogens, in-flammables or other toxic and volatile substances. Biosafety cabinets provide a safe environment for research involving infectious microorganisms or other harmful particulates.
Before use to check the lighting, the ventilation system is normal, will be used on both sides of the cabinet.
Pull the glass window down to your elbow during experiment to allow air to pass underneath.
Laboratory should often be ventilated even though lab fume hood is not used, it is beneficial to the health of the test personnel.
When more than two chemical fume hoods share one fan, the "on" and "off" of the fan can only be controlled by one operator to avoid improper operation. If another ventilation cabinet is temporarily not used or stopped using, the air volume control valve can be used to close the vent, to avoid repeating "on" and "off" the fan.
Open Windows for 10 minutes every 2 hours for ventilation. Use time more than 5 hours, to open the window, to avoid negative pressure indoor.
After the experiment, the exhaust fan should continue to run for several minutes, so that the exhaust gas in the cabinet is completely removed.
If appears malfunction, close the cabinet door immediately and contact the maintenance personnel.
The work surface must be cleaned after each use.
