The Nubico ebook service is bought by the Swedish company Nextory
The Spanish ebook service, Nubic, which belongs to Telefonica and they worked with Grupo Planeta to offer the service, has been sold to the Swedish company Nextory, a service of ebooks and audioebooks that through this purchase will reach Spain.
Thus, Nextory plans to land in Spain permanently before the end of the year and with it a catalog of nearly 600.000 titles, including ebooks and audioebooks.
Nubico is an ebook service via streaming or flat rate ebooks that was born in Spain years ago and that thanks to agreements with Movistar and other companies has managed to reach many Spanish homes. Movistar users had a price reduction or a few more days of trial and non-Movistar users had a shorter trial period.
While it is true that we have no news that Nubico was an overwhelming success like other streaming services are, such as Netflix, it was unknown that it was a loss or that it would give Movistar and Grupo Planeta losses.
Nextory, the future name of Nubico, is a flat-rate service that in addition to ebooks has audioebooks, used through smartphone app and offers three prices that contain certain characteristics. The Nextory catalog is contains more than 600.000 titles that are distributed between ebooks and audiobooks or audioebooks.
A lower price, around 16 euros, would mean having unlimited access to the catalog and several profiles, but there could only be one profile using the platform, that is, two users could not read at the same time. And finally the third price, the lowest, would be almost 13 euros and it would be for a single profile and would have 30 hours a month to reproduce the catalog.
I understand that the difference between the current Nubico and Nextory will disappear in favor of Nubico and that we will have the benefits of Nextory, that is, a service for families and a catalog of audioebooks for a price similar or equal to the current cost of Nubico, but We have to say that at the moment nothing has been officially reported (in addition to what has been discussed) about the changes in the services, on the other hand logical and normal.
