The popular novelist and scholar Arturo Pérez-Reverte has been in charge of adapting the work for school use. This peculiar edition of the best-known work in Spanish literature will be published by Santillana in all Spanish-speaking countries, and will be on sale on November 29.
These words bear the signature of Pérez-Reverte who has made an adaptation of the work allowing the work to be read linearly and respecting the integrity of the text. What's more They will see original and unpublished drawings, among which we can find one by Francisco de Goya which was never included in the 1780 edition and when at that time the painter did not have much of a reputation.
As can be read in a press release from the RAE, the work of Arturo Pérez Reverte “reveals to readers the essence, the heart of the classic of world literature. With an impeccable revision work, this new edition offers for the first time a linear reading of the central plot of “Don Quixote”, respecting the integrity of the text, the fundamental episodes, the tone and the general structure of the work ”.
