I have been testing this device for the last few months thanks to the guys at Energy Sistem. It is the first Android ereader I tried and now we will see what I thought
First I leave the technical data so that you can see its characteristics and then I will tell you about the sensations that it has caused me and what I think of this device.
The device we It arrives very well presented, with a robust and beautiful box and an interior with details that make a very good first impression. The black dust jacket with the heart of Enegy sistem that protects the device when opening the case, the velvety bottom, etc.
The back is made of smooth plastic and its appearance deceives us, because it seems that it is going to slip but really good grip. We can hold it with one hand perfectly without touching the touch screen by mistake.
We can read well and enjoy but when we compare with other well-known brands is when we see the differences and that point that it lacks to be a great ereader. Despite the soda if we look we notice that ink background with the letters that was before and lacks a bit of contrast
At the battery level, it perfectly fulfills what an ereader is, forgetting in several weeks to have to recharge. Not being enlightened helps a lot.
It is the first reader with Android that I try and the truth is that I was surprised by its possibilities.
Each gadget has a different function and the ereaders are for reading, but being able to use the Play Store applications allows us to connect with social networks and be able to send information to the ereader. Thanks to Android we can enjoy a large number of applications and integrations to our readings.
But where we can really take advantage of it is when sending information to the ereader. We can use Pocket, drive, mail, we can send books, documents or read articles that we have marked from our PC browser, laptop or smartphone.
A correct ereader with which you will enjoy your readings, but it is not a device for the most demanding or comparable to the high ranges. Android gives you very interesting use options that are not possible in conventional ereaders, but it lacks the screen and the fluidity when using it.
Last week Amazon announced the official launch in Spain and other countries of the Kindle Voyage, after a long wait. It also announced by surprise a new Kindle Paperwhite that replaces the one that had been on the market until now, which is still sold in many stores or department stores and which has some very interesting improvement that we are going to review through this article in which we can face to face the new and the old Kindle Paperwhite.
We are going to start by reviewing the main features and specifications of the Kindle Paperwhite that until recently was sold in the market. Remember that here you can see the review we made of this device.
Inclusion of the Kindle Page Flip reading function that will allow users to flip through books by page, jump from one chapter to another or even jump to the end of the book without losing the reading point
If we look at the characteristics of each of the two devices, soon we will be able to realize that the improvements are not too many, but they are important. Starting with the screen, it has improved greatly, with a resolution of 300 dpi, the company directed by Jeff Bezos promises us that reading on this new Kindle Paperwhite will be like doing it on paper.
Even the weight is exactly the same between the two Kindle. Finally, to the novelties that we already find in the old Kindle Paperwhite, we now add the inclusion of the exclusive Amazon font named Bookerly and that will allow us a simpler and more comfortable reading.
Stunning 300 dpi high resolution display - reads like paper, without glare, even in bright sunlight.
I fell in love with the Kindle Paperwhite the same day that I tried it and I can't see a day when the new Kindle can prove that its improved screen can offer us a reading experience simply unmatched.
