On June 26, 1997 an unknown JK Rowling published the first novel of the Harry Potter sagaEntitled harry potter and the Philosopher's Stone, which very soon became a success and is now nothing less than 20 years old. The rest of the story is well known to almost everyone, with the arrival of six more books in bookstores, in addition to many additions to the margin of the saga, in the form of books, movies and many other things.
To celebrate the passing of time and the birthday of one of the greatest literary phenomena in history, we are going to review 20 curiosities about the best known magician of all time and the entire universe that surrounds him. We will not only limit ourselves to the book saga, but we will also tell you some curiosity about the movies and the many texts published by Rowling about her magical world.
1 20 curiosities about the best known magician of all time
1.18 The scared of Professor McGonagall's cat
Next we tell you the curiosities about Harry Potter and his entire universe that surely you did not know;
JK Rowling and Harry Potter have the same birthday, on July 31, although in the case of the writer from 19565 and in the case of the magician from 1980. The curiosity goes further and is that Daniel Radcliffe, the actor who plays Harry in the different films, also has his birthday on the same day .
The last name Potter was chosen by the British writer inspired by her neighbors, and is that the Potters were a family that lived four houses beyond where Rowling lived when she was still a child. Of course, at the moment and after so long his neighbors have said absolutely nothing, and we also do not know that they thought that Rowling used his last name to put it to the most famous magician of all time.
Hogwarts is the best-known school of magic and sorcery, but it is not the only one and there are a total of 11 schools of magic spread throughout the world. As can be read in books we know Hogwarts located in Scotland, Beauxbatons in France, Durmstrag in Germany, Ouagadou, in the mountains of the Moon in Africa, Mahoutokoro, on a small volcanic island in Japan and Ilvermore, located in the United States.
The books never talk about the sexuality of Dumbledore, the director of Hogwarts, although in the sixth film JK Rowling herself had to make a correction to prevent a love story between a girl and the director from appearing. The writer did not consider it necessary to talk about Dumbledore's sexuality, but she was always clear that he was a gay character.
Hermione, in a further display of her abilities and determination, returned to Hogwarts to finish her studies and get her Ecstasy title. Harry and Ron, for their part, never did it, staying without achieving the desired title, although in view of the events it would have been of little use to them.
A boggart that is in the presence of Voldemort would transform into his corpse, and it is that what the dark lord fears most is his own death. Who now dares to face one of the most terrible and hated beings in literature?
Si a muggle found hogwarts, something quite unlikely, the only thing he would see would be a castle and a lonely sign that he would put up; "Get away!
Ron's second life Ron had two lives thanks to JK Rowling's change of mind and is that the writer was about to kill the good of RON in the middle of the saga as she herself has told on several occasions.
One of the great landmarks of Harry Potter's life is the Battle of Hogwarts which takes place in 1998, the very year in which the first book was published. The theories of this are very varied, although JK Rowling has never told us about this strange date.
After defeating Voldemort at the end of the last book in the literary saga, Harry Potter loses the ability to speak Parseltongue. This is explained by the fact that the little wizard is no longer attached to the dark lord.
Harry Potter not only took care of his children and is that Teddy Lupine, the son of Remus and TonksHe was raised by his grandmother, but on a large number of occasions he stayed to sleep at the house of his godfather who was none other than Harry.
They say animals and children always give a lot of trouble to film crews, and in one of the Harry Potter movies there was a problem with the gamut playing Professor McGonagall. It disappeared at one point and they never managed to find it again, having to replace it with another.
One thing not many people know is that neither Neville and Gilderoy Lockhart's parents were never able to recover from magical conditions. And there are things that dark magic does that nobody or nothing can cure.
Harry Potter never forgot Snape and his heroism, and one example of this is that he fought and managed to have his portrait as Headmaster of Hogwarts restored in its rightful place and from which it should never have moved.
Do you know any shocking curiosity of Harry Potter and the entire universe that surrounds it?. Tell us in the space reserved for comments on this entry, in our forum or through one of the social networks in which we are present and eager to read everything you have to tell us.
Two days ago E-ink has announced its new panel electronic ink, in which color takes center stage and the truth is that it was not expected that it could present a technology that surpasses the color quality of a printer.
Slashgear has been able to get very close to E-ink's new Advanced Color ePaper (ACeP). This new epaper distances itself from the color filter required in previous screens of this type and, instead, displays a full range of colors, which includes the primary colors by using the colored pigments in each pixel.
The flash that you can see is due to how the screen prepares for the activation of another color. Which means that thanks to those 8 color pigments, the refresh rate is very low, and that is why we will not see these panels in an eReader.
The vast majority of ePubs, mobis and equivalents, are monochromatic (if we do not take their covers into account), the exception being illustrated books or with photographs, the former generally for children and the latter for art.
That is why I suspect that our area of interest is the one that least worries the manufacturers of this product.
But this is ultimately not so, and possibly for 2018 let's see the first eReaders with ACEP screens, as has been confirmed from several sources that have mentioned that until that year, we will not see the mass production of these panels for any company that wants to use them for their digital readers and smartphones. The first products to take advantage of this new technology, called Advanced Color E-paper, will be those aimed at digital signage.
And surely some of the big companies are already looking at the possibilities of ACEP for their devices. Also on the side that touches the monitors, the integration of a panel of these characteristics would be very interesting for certain professionals who spend hours and hours in front of a screen in the day.
So we will not lose what we wrote down. Marvin is also compatible with interactive ebooks in addition to the epub formatThis is thanks to its compatibility with services such as Google Maps, Wikipedia, Facebook, Goodreads, etc ... Services that many of us use and that will allow interactive ebooks to function properly.
I am not a user of that system, but it is interesting to output the latest versions of the ebook. I have read that gyan reader is the most advanced.
