I have been very good this year and, because of being magicians, I know that you can give me the gift I ask for. I have to confess that I love any of my readers madly, they have their flaws, but all of them have provided me with many hours of entertainment and I do not want to be ungrateful.
Well, very simple, surely you all know what I mean, because you will not deny me that at some point I will not have you imagined the ideal reader, the one that has everything that seems best to us of all the readers we know and some that we invent, the one that has that function that at one point we have missed while reading, the one that populates our fantasies and winks at us from some corner of our imagination.
If we go to a big reader, weight is the big drawback, because everyone I know is around half a kilo, but as it is ideal and dreamlike, we can make it slim, ethereal, made with cloud nanoparticles ... Be realistic, Irene, that weighs at least 250 grams because ask for a weight similar to that of the PRS -T1 or T2 would be reckless, not even the Magi could achieve it. In when the Storage capacityI would ask for unlimited, but one thing is to dream and another to speak nonsense.
With this I am not saying that the plastic ones are not acceptable, in fact, they are to some extent responsible for the cheaper devices, but I prefer aluminum. And, given the choice, I will choose something that I like about the Papyre or the Sony T1 and T2, the colors, that each one can decide the color you really like, not just the most common gray, white and black.
About the light I have not decided yet, in principle I would settle for a nice extra lamp that does not produce uncomfortable reflections. Although if a decent, uniform front lighting was achieved, without reflections or darker areas, the option would be very interesting.
A feature that not all readers include but that is extremely interesting is the text-to-speech, which is nothing more than the ability of the reader to "read" aloud each of the books. So I want it, and that it doesn't sound tinny, but that it be a natural voice.
And finally, I want a cool case, like the ones from Tuff-Luv, but of course, as he will not be a traditional reader, it will be difficult to find a cover that fits him perfectly. The same thing to do a franken case for a franken reader.
As you have seen, it is an article to express dreams, so feel free to do so. What characteristics would your ideal reader have?
