Why did Sony “give away” the case on its Sony Reader PRS-T3?
The question is the one that gives title to this article; Why did Sony “give away” the case on its Sony Reader PRS-T3?and to which as I said I have not been able to give an answer but through this article I will try to draw some conclusion.
With the arrival of the Sony Reader PRS-T3, the cover is already included with the electronic book so it will not be necessary to acquire it with what Sony loses one of its main income, which is certainly difficult for me to understand since no company in the digital reading market offers a case with its device and I do not see the reason why it is signed Japanese should offer it.
The conclusion could be that Sony cares little about the benefits of the eReader market, very likely conclusion or that the benefits offered by these devices are so great that you do not mind offering your users a cover included in the device.
