A couple of years ago I bought my mother an e-book. I have developed certain moral objections, so to speak, towards Amazon, since I bought my first Kindle: both at the level of the prices of their books (ebooks more expensive than paper books), and because of their aggressive policy of wanting to eat the world, or the conditions in which its employees work (look what happened to the Spanish who have emigrated to Germany and ended up working at Amazon ...)
So, without thinking about it, the moral to take the ass and Kindle to the song!
Do not hang, or reinstall, or technical service ... The only thing you have to be careful with is with the cat ...
And don't get me wrong: those of you who have one and are satisfied with it, what luck and I'm happy for you!
And so the odyssey began ... hang up when turning the light up / down, hang up when activating / deactivating the wifi, hang up when changing the letter, hang up when turning the page, hang up WHILE IT WAS TURNED ON ... To give you an idea, during its first day of use, the record time without crashing should be around 3 minutes ...
I don't even dare to think about what will happen if the same happens with the replacement. I can see myself with a 130 € sausage cutting board ...
That after that time, the brand has not learned anything and continues to have the face of marketing products that they KNOW fail so often seems unfortunate, both on the part of BQ and Fnac. And even more so the fact that, being aware of the failures, complaints and claims, the Fnac has taken the liberty of censoring negative comments on its website, knowing that as ALL negative comments were published, they would not sell a single one.
