The eReaders have provided us with an interesting option, which for many goes unnoticed, but which many others value very much. I am talking about the function that, for example, the Kindle has show us the approximate time we have left to finish reading a book.
The times that it shows us for all the books are for an average reader, and that has a reading speed of 300 words per minute. However, if you think that you cannot read the number of words per minute or that you even read some more every 60 seconds, it does not matter, since you will be able to quantify the words that you are able to read and the service itself will recalculate the time it will take for you to finish reading a certain book.
I don't know what it will look like to you, but the truth is that that time is quite short for me, since this novel is not exactly short, but perhaps I will even read it again to know the precision that howlongtoreadthis offers us.
