Last week Sony presented its new eReader that promises new and interesting improvements and which he has baptized following almost a tradition as Sony Reader PRS-T3. Of this new device we have already reviewed many of its aspects such as the specifications or characteristics but every day that passes I ask myself a question to which I cannot give a firm answer.
And it is that if Amazon obtains its benefits through the sale of different digital content, Sony makes all its profits from the sale of its devices and in the case of the PRS-T1 and PRS-T2 through their different covers, very necessary and sold at sometimes abusive prices.
I have thought that it could be a way to differentiate itself from other companies but the loss is very important since, for example, the Sony Reader PRS-T2 cover was worth between 35 and 50 euros depending on the model that was chosen.
Why do you think Sony decided to include a cover in its new Sony Reader PRS-T3?.
I think it may be a set of all three.
Well, it is clear that the case it provides does not have a light, that the device itself does not have LED backlighting and that the case with external lighting will be sold separately for 50 euros, so you can not use the current case included. The device costs 150 euros.
I am inclined to think that the «cover» has a durability in time of x…. With which, in the medium term, if you have to open and close the book many times, since the reading is synchronized with the sleep mode when opening and closing, as you run out of cover, you can throw the book away.
Also the Spanish dictionary that is integrated (I suppose due to user demand), although its support page for books is still non-existent.
I don't see a big loss, as far as the "sleeve" is a competitor to Amazon. Rather, I see that the "hare" is taken by Sony, because she eats and cooks the "case" by herself without having intermediaries, that they take the profits from the case in question.
The light does not really provide great clarity in a case ... I think that reading with a suitable light source is preferable to having to leave your eyes with an "optical mini-lens", which gives you some light to read.
Another drawback that I see, is that with the PRICE that the reader has, it should be able to come with a current charger (I have looked for an adapter, because his costs an hour ... of monkey and another of duck) and with That's Easter, but… they could have rounded the market share more, in addition to the improvements implemented, with the POWER ADAPTER.
