To do this, in the configuration menu, select the option "Update the Kindle".
First of all we must move from the root directory of the Kindle to our computer the file "DONT_HALT_ON_REPAIR”. At the end of installing Duokan we can delete them since the device should create it when it restarts.
In the next menu that will appear we must select the option "Disable Diagnostics"and then the option "To continue ".
To translate Duokan into English or Spanish, we must edit the file "DK_system \ xKindle \ config.ini "with the PSPAD editor (You will find the download link at the end of the article in the "Download" section). At the end of the file we will addLanguage = 2if we want to enjoy part of the menus in English orLanguage = 8if we prefer Spanish.
Notice: It is totally normal that even if we change the language, Chinese epigraphs appear since it is not yet fully translated.
