More and more people decide to start reading in English for different reasons, among which we could include improved compression, professional reasons or simply because there are no translations available for reading. Today for all those who read in English we want to offer you 6 books to start reading in English, although before starting with this list of books we want to make it clear that they are not books for beginners or people without previous knowledge.
2 Lord of the Flies by William Golding
El Ernest Hemingway's latest work of fiction it is probably his best known novel and one that has managed to rank among the most widely read books in history. In it, a Santiago fisherman who lives in Havana, where he cannot catch practically anything, is one fine day surprised by a swordfish that bites the hook, entering a story that you should not miss, in English or any other language.
Lord of the Flies o Lord of the Flies It is the first and best known novel by William Golding that was published in 1954. Although it is a classic of English literature, it is not well known in other countries, but we have decided to recommend it since it will not leave anyone indifferent.
Reading this novel in English is doing us a great favor, and it is that despite the fact that the translations are very elaborate and are quite exact, in many passages of the novel something of the essence that Orwell wanted to give to his story is lost.
Frankenstein or the modern Prometheus It is a novel that many have decided to frame in the tradition of the Gothic novel. Surely no one needs us to talk or tell them anything about this story, but in case you just woke up from a deep sleep we can tell you that in this story the protagonist tries to rival God.
