The last example is the Kobo Aura H2O Edition 2, an updated and improved version of the Kobo Aura Edition 2 that the company launched on the market a few months ago. Available worldwide offers us a more than good experience to enjoy digital reading, also offering us resistance to water that will even allow us to submerge it to two meters deep for two hours, and a new feature called ComfortLight PRO which reduces exposure to blue light so that we can read more comfortably in the dark.
3 Our experience when reading
It is available in the always sober black color, with the only color tint on the power button, located on the back, and which is blue. At the moment Kobo has not confirmed if it will launch more colors on the market, something that many of us would surely appreciate for not always living in the seriousness of black.
It is not recommended, but we can also experiment with reading underwater, something that will be tremendously difficult for anyone. Finally, when it comes to design and manufacturing, we cannot overlook the weight of this device, which is 207 grams, which makes it one of the heaviest eReaders on the market in terms of numbers, although once we have the device in hand, it is not a burden that "bothers us" when it comes to enjoying digital reading.
Here we show you the Main features and specifications of the new Kobo Aura H2O Edition 2;
Front lighting: ComfortLigth PRO that reduces exposure to blue light for a much more comfortable night reading
Without a doubt, one of the most outstanding features of this new Kobo device is its 6.8-inch screen, which allows us to enjoy books in digital format with practically the same size as books in the traditional paper format. In addition, we should also highlight the front lighting of the device, which has ComfortLight PRO technology and which reduces exposure to blue light, which in turn allows us to read in very dark situations without our eyes suffering or directly hurting us .
Today it is not too normal to find electronic books with such large screens on the market, but it is undoubtedly a great advantage to be able to enjoy digital books on a 6.8-inch screen. It is not as big as the Kobo Aura, but its size is more than enough to have a much better experience than we can have with any device with a 6-inch screen or even less.
We are talking about the ComfortLight PRO feature that reduces exposure to blue light and that is regulated depending on the light that is in the environment so that at all times it is very comfortable to enjoy reading. Explained in a simple way, we could say that if we read outdoors, the light will be much more intense and if we read in the dark the degree of luminosity will be reduced so that our eyes do not end up tired.
In addition, this new device combines several very interesting features, which make this Kobo Aura H2O 2017 a very interesting electronic book. We are talking about the huge screen that it offers us, the possibility of wetting it, something that is ideal for these summer days, and the speed with which we can handle ourselves through the user interface and through the different digital books that we are enjoying .
