This new eReader had already been tracked thanks to the FCC registration but everyone thought it would be called Kobo Aura One 2 or Kobo Aura Two, but the name changed, as well as its shape. The new Kobo Forma is an eReader with a different name and a totally different form.
The Kobo Forma allows one-handed reading as well as control of the device with a couple of finger taps. And unlike other models, Kobo Forma allows screen flipping, which means that we can change the direction and thus help the reading of pdf documents.
The screen as well as the rest of the device has Moebius technology that makes the screen not only more resistant but also a more flexible and resistant device. The Kobo Forma continues to count, like its older brothers, with the IPX8 certificate that makes the device resistant to shocks, scratches and water.
The price of the Kobo Forma will be 279,99 euros, 30 euros more expensive than the Kindle Oasis. The price is not at all affordable when compared to a normal eReader, but we have to say that the Kobo Forma is not a normal or low-end eReader, but a premium device, so the quality / price ratio is quite balanced.
Soon we will analyze this new Kobo device on our website, but it seems that everything indicates that Kobo remains a great rival to crack. Do not you think?
