It is reported that users can no longer access content purchased through this platform. Bad news for those who have purchased an eBook through this Microsoft store.
What you are actually buying is the license that allows you to read the book through digital rights management. The DRM, as it is known in English, is what regulates copyright licenses, it was linked to the Microsoft book store server.
No specific date has been given in July for the closure of this eBook store. Therefore, the recommendation for users is to act as soon as possible, contact Microsoft or read the email well, to find out how they should get this refund.
After many months of waiting, Amazon put its new Kindle Voyage on sale last week, an eReader that we could qualify as Premium, in Spain and many other countries around the world. This device is nothing new since it has already been sold for a long time in countries such as the United States, the United Kingdom or Germany, but it is something new for all Spanish users.
In this article we are going to put the new Kindle Paperwhite and the Kindle Voyage face to face so that you discover all their similarities and differences and you can decide whether to acquire one or the other.
If we take a look at the features and specifications of each device, we can quickly realize that the differences between the two eReaders are minimal.
As we already said the only different point is the design, where the Voyage stands out widely with its very careful finishes, its premium materials and a slightly lower weight than the new Kindle Paperwhite that however we are not going to notice to a great extent.
We continue with the complicated answer questions, and it is that here it will depend a lot on the budget we have and if we are willing to pay a few euros more for having a little more power, which will be practically priceless, and a very careful and different design.
