While not long ago Kobo presented its new device called Kobo Ellipsa, the Geniatech company has presented a similar model but with some extra functions and features that seem interesting. Geniatech is a company of Chinese origin that was founded in Beijing 24 years ago and is currently located in the technological Shenzhen area.
Geniatech has officially presented its KloudNote device that can be bought and stored in our home in the coming days. The Kloudnote is an ereader in the shape of a digital notebook, that is, an A4-size screen and accompanied by a stylus to help us use the device as a digital notebook.
We miss a backlit screen, but it is also true that if we use it to write, the light does not have to be a problem in these scenarios. Kloudnote does not have a capped or embedded operating system but uses Android 8.1, a fairly recent version that will allow us to have extra functions that other devices do not have.
KloudNote measurements are 250 x 175 x 7.6mm with a weight of 385 gr., quite reasonable for those who want to use it as an ebook reader and quite light for those who want to use it as a work tool.
This port is accompanied by a wifi-bluetooth module that allows us to connect to the internet and be able to listen to audio books through wireless headphones. At the bottom of the device we will find a 3.5mm minijack port that will also allow us to connect headphones by wire and to these two ways of listening to audio formats we have to add the classic speaker option that Kloudnote also has.
Having Android 8.1, the range of formats that the device supports is very wide and although in the specifications, Geniatech talks about the basics, we can think that all the ebook formats compatible with Android and even the most famous library apps for Android can be used on this device even though do not talk at all about the Play Store.
On the latter we do not know more than the official information and we do not know if it will be compatible with all computers or we will need a USB-C type cable for its connection but it sounds interesting. Nor do we know anything about the type of cloud that we will use, what limitations it has (such as the price for the use of this service) or if it is compatible with other more popular cloud services that allows us to have everything in an orderly and concentrated way.
The price of the Kloudnote will be $ 449 and can be reserved through its Official Site. However, we still do not know when the final launch and sale date of this device will be, as well as in the countries where it can be sold.
