Together with Kindle Travel the company directed by Jeff Bezos also officially launched a new Kindle Paperwhite with some other improvement, especially on its screen. These two new devices can put in great doubt any user who will have to decide between two devices that seem similar, but that are very different in terms of characteristics and above all price.
First of all, we are going to review the main features and specifications of both devices;
3 Is the difference between the two devices real and palpable?
Screen: incorporates a 6-inch screen with letter e-papper technology, touch, with a resolution of 1440 x 1080 and 300 pixels per inch
Higher screen contrast that will allow us to read in a more comfortable and pleasant way
The screens have the same size and the same resolution. Internally, Amazon does not provide much information, but from what we have been able to find out, they are two very similar devices.
Which one do I buy?
There is no doubt that we are dealing with two electronic books of enormous quality and that they would win in almost any comparison to other devices of this type on the market. Amazon has created two almost perfect eReaders, which differ mainly in their design and that they are indicated for users who like to enjoy digital reading, and for those who, in addition to reading, also want to enjoy design and the best materials.
The Voyage is lighter, something that is appreciated the truth, and more beautiful because the screen is at the same height as the bezel. Other differences are the light sensor that the Voyage includes and the physical buttons ...
A good comparison is made with the two devices in hand. The difference is not only aesthetic, you have not commented anything about the pressure sensor, or the difference in weight, or the self-regulating light ... or the sensation of one and the other when holding it in your hand.
