Apparently the latest firmware update for the device (1.0.05.12140) comes with a surprise: after installing it it is impossible to root the device (at least for now).
You can decide to do not root it, so you install the update with complete peace of mind (this one, for now, has no going back).
You can wait to make the decision and, if you want to root it, do it before updating the firmware (in case the second option has not already been given).
Normally a new firmware can solve security problems, improve performance or provide new functions, precisely for that reason I do not say that it is not installed, simply that you keep in mind that, at least for the moment, after installing it you will not be able to root your device. In the case of this firmware, the highlight is that improves the display of ePUB content.
Tutorial: Remove DRM from Kindle eBooks
Download the caliber completes that are included in DRM Removal Tools for eBooks
Select the first of the .zip files in it and open it. The way to open the file will depend on the program to decompress files that you will have installed
Click on Accept in the next dialog box that will appear
When you have downloaded all the electronic books you want or all the ones you want to check out, go back to Caliber and choose the option; Add books from directories, including subdirectories
It's important to remember:
It is as if you buy a book, made of paper, and you can only read it at home, and you cannot take it out of it. By removing that restriction (DRM), you could take the book out and take it wherever you want.
