In recent days, flat book rates are very up-to-date, among which is the Amazon Kindle Unlimited, which we have been testing in the last days thanks to the 30-day free trial that Amazon offers to all users. In this article I am going to tell you about my experience with the service and I am also going to expose what I think are the positive and negative points of it.
Before expressing my opinion about the service, I think we can start with the positive and negative points of this new Amazon reading service:
Su price is undoubtedly one of its attractions, since for the amount of 9,99 euros you can access more than 700.000 books
One of the most positive points is the possibility of accessing the service from eReaders, smartphones and tablets And that does not limit you to having to buy the books in a single device. For example, it is possible to buy books very easily from a Kindle Paperwhite
The option of not being able to use this service on other eReaders the market limits it a bit
In my case, for example, I do not have a Kindle, so I can only take advantage of this service on my smartphone and on my tablet, which I sincerely believe is not worth it. It is true that you could download the "purchased" books, convert them to another format and put them in another eReader, but this would be a job that you would not have to do with another service of this type.
Have you tried the new Kindle Unlimited service? What is your opinion about it?.
The good thing about the service is that for € 10 you can "take a look" at books that you wouldn't normally buy. Anyway, it all depends on how much or how little a reader you are to make it worth it or not.
On the other hand, it is true that it can only be used with a kindle ereader, but it is also valid for PCs and tablets from other brands.
But the most negative point of all, in my view, is that the subscription is automatically renewed once the trial month is over. I do not know to what extent this will be legal but immoral of course it is for a while.
