They are books that the American politician has read a short time ago, and that he recommends reading to everyone. We have already read some of them, but with a certain wickedness the question arises as to whether the new President Trump will read any of them.
1 Warrior woman
5 A bend in the river
7 Solomon's song
9 The underground railway
Barack Obama's first recommendation is Warrior womanA work of Maxine hong kingston where we are told the story of an American woman, with Chinese ancestry and a large collection of opinions about Asian myths, Chinese families and the events of her childhood in her new life in California.
It is one of the best-selling books worldwide and has been translated in a huge number of languages. It is also the quintessential work of the Nobel Prize along with possibly A Chronicle of a Death Foretoldo Memory of my sad whores.
China is undoubtedly one of Obama's great interests, at least when it comes to literature. A sample of it is the work The three-body problem where the role of science in our societies is exposed, which greatly helps us understand what happened in the past and what will happen in the future in the Asian country.
In the hands of the furies
To know the less good part of this story of adolescent love, you must pay attention to Obama and read In the hands of the furies.
Obama's African roots could not fail to be present in this interesting list of books that he has proposed to us, and he shows it with his work A bend in the river, where the effects of policies are narrated, in the turbulent period of the independence of an African country, in the lives of individuals.
Gone girl Without a doubt This is the recommendation of Barack Obama that I like the most, although I can say that I like all the others very much as well, but this novel by Gillyan Flyan will hook you from the first moment and will make you not stop reading.
The narrative mixes between fantasy and the harsh reality of the black ghettos of the sixties. Perhaps with this the former president of the United States tries to make known part of the history, which already seems forgotten for many, and which unfortunately is still present not only in some neighborhoods of the North American country, but neighborhoods around the world.
Just by reading some of the criticism that the novel has received throughout history The naked and the dead, one can realize the category that this book has. Rated by many as the best war novel written in this century and placing its author, Norman Mailer, at the height of Tolstoy or Hemingway, one can quickly realize the adventure on which we are going to embark.
“A black notebook, in which is Anna Wulf, the writer; a red notebook, dedicated to politics; a yellow one, in which I write stories that come from my experience, and a blue notebook that tries to be a diary "
Awarded with the Pulitzer 2005 and the National Book Critic Circles Award, this work served to elevate Marilynne Robinson as one of the most relevant and well-known writers, not only in the United States, but throughout the world, where her works have been translated into a huge number of different languages.
