I have tried to fiddle with the gadget to see what changes could be made (include voices in Spanish, choose languages based on the language the book is in, etc.) but, although I think I already know where the voices are, I don't know I dare to fiddle a lot lest the invention explode and I am left without a voice in English and without a voice in Spanish and without a reader.
If any of you are looking for readers with TTS function, I leave you one little list so you can start choosing. I include the discontinued ones in case you have the opportunity to acquire them second-hand at a good price.
EnTourage Pocket eDGe launched in 2010 and discontinued in 2011 (although still distributed in Russia), with 6 ”e-ink screen with 16 gray levels (along with an LCD screen).
Samsung Papyrus, launched in 2009, with 5 ″ electronic ink screen and 8 levels of gray.
