One of the most complicated processes to carry out with Amazon devices is to order and organize the book collections that we have stored on our device. That is why today we are going to show you an interesting application, calledkindlean, that will allow us to order our books in a very comfortable, fast and above all simple way.
Once we have installed the application on our Kindle, we must run it and she will take care of scanning the content for a few seconds that we have saved in the different memories and it will show us all the data with a very similar aspect to that shown in the following photo.
If we want add a book to a specific collection It will be enough to drag it to it and from that moment on we will have it incorporated. We can also edit all the labels we want for each book, from the pot, to the author or publisher.
Surely once you try this interesting application you will not be able to stop using it. For those of you who have never used it, you should know that there are two versions of this application, a free download and a premium one for which we will have to pay $ 19,95, about 15 euros.
Until now I only used caliber, and even though it is a great tool, it seemed somewhat crude to use for content management. With Kindlean, everything so visual and fast, it really is a pleasure to put order in our entire electronic library.
