As I always say, I like to see the packaging because it seems to me a declaration of intentions of what we are going to enter into and the truth is that the Likebook Mars comes very well prepared. With a nice design and rigid box.
The back is made of smooth plastic and although it does not slip, a grip is missed rather than a safety one. As I said, it seems that the cover gives you an extra security when it comes to picking it up.
The Likebook has WIFI, bluetooth and reads microSD cards up to 64Gb. It also comes with a tool installed to transfer files via wifi from a pc or device connected to the same network.
The 3200 mAh battery will give us joy for several weeks. I have only tested the device in reading mode and some Android apps, if we listen to music or intensive use of the screen with an application, I do not know how it will respond.
I was really surprised by the Likebook Mars and I am not surprised that it is considered, as I said at the beginning in many media, as one of the best or the best ereader of 2018. The use of Android makes it a multi-tool, and makes make it tremendously useful.
I would like to see this device with a better grip design, just like the Oasis and the Kobo Forma do.
