So that you can know well what Caliber Portable is and also what we can use it for and how it works.. Thus, if it turns out that it is something of your interest, you can get the most out of it.
What it does is store the books in a database and then allows us to search very precisely what we are looking for. We can generally store books based on many different parameters such as title, author, publisher, or publication date.
So it is a tool that stands out for its versatility, since the absolute majority of users can make use of it. Since it supports the main eBook formats that are handled today.
We can configure it so that it takes care of searching and automatically sends us news from various sites. It is not possible to do it with all the websites, simply with some with which the company has an agreement.
Kovid Goyal is the creator and founder of the company. One of the reasons for the creation of the company is that at that time there were no quality tools that allowed you convert files to the LRF format that Sony readers used at that moment.
Thus, decided to develop an interface that would make it easier to organize all e-books that you had stored on your eReader. This became what we now know as the Caliber Portable.
The program is constantly updated, in fact the last update was at the end of March. Therefore, improvements are introduced on a regular basis, in addition to security improvements.
The official website is not the only place where Caliber Portable is available. Because there are other many web pages for downloading programs such as Softonic or CCM where we can download it.
You can organize all your eBooks in a simple way and so it will be much more convenient for you to find everything you have stored on your device. In addition, we can organize the books according to the parameter we want (author, title, publisher, publication date, ISBN ...).
We can also send them to another device very comfortably, our eReader in this case or even an iPhone or iPad. Something that shows us that it is a very versatile tool and that it gives us many possibilities.
Currently I cannot imagine having a personal library of e-books without this program.
It is a bigger screen but without being anything excessive. Possibly from here we can say that an ereader is great.
