2 The time has come to do some simple math operations
Let's first take a look at the statistics that have been used to conclude that up to 200 books can be read per year;
Most of the books have about 50.000 words on average, although it goes without saying that there are books with many more words and with many fewer, even if we did not make an average it would be impossible to carry out these calculations. The time has come to do some simple math operations
If it seems impossible to you to be able to sit and enjoy a book for 417 hours a year, keep in mind that most of us spend 1.642 hours watching television or 608 hours viewing and interacting on social networks.
This study refers to North American people, although all the data could be extended to anyone and of course also to Spaniards. That if we are capable does not mean that we do it and more considering that only three people out of ten claim to read regularly.
I am convinced that if we set our minds to it, we could read a book a day, and therefore 365 books a year, but surely we would not enjoy or savor them as a book should. Our recommendation is that you read for pleasure without setting a goal to read a certain number of books and that you end up leaving yourself apart from the beauty of reading.
Mathematics says that 200
Continuing with the operations, 417 hours: 200 books = 2 hours and 5 minutes per book. And a question comes to me: only 2 hours for each book?
Personally, after finding blogs in which you set your own reading challenges, by 2016 I had proposed 50 books, and I reached 52, enjoying reading. The problem is that many novels, especially historical ones, do not go below 700-800 pages.
It is best to aim to read a reasonable minimum of books per year. For example, this year I took on a 40-book reading challenge, and to make it more interesting, each one must fit into a specific category (A book written by a person of color, a book that involves travel, a book that is go to make film).
I don't know where those calculations came from.
In fact, there are some other books that could have saved me.
