Books that Obama recommends us to read and enjoy | All eReaders
The already former president Barack Obama He is an avid reader, something that he has shown on more than one occasion and that he also tells us in his book Dreams from my father, where he narrates that some of the weekends in which he does not work, he relaxes in an apartment of his property where his only companions are books. Now that history is already formed has once again displayed his good taste when it comes to literature and has offered us a recommendation of 11 books.
2 One hundred years of loneliness
4 In the hands of the furies
8 The naked and the dead
From these events his new identity is built, which is perfectly reflected in this book.
One Hundred Years of Solitude It is one of the great classics of world literature and that of course the former president of the United States has not wanted to stop including in his list of books. Gabriel García Márquez signs this book in which we can discover in great detail the adventures of the Buendía-Iguarán family.
The election of the American politician is not a coincidence and it is that this work is considered one of the great master leftovers of literature And it has received very positive reviews from a huge number of experts and ordinary readers.
The best known work of Lauren groff tell us the passion story between Lotto and Mathilde of twenty-two years, who have just gotten married without hardly knowing each other and that goes on in time for a great number of years. Unfortunately the harsh reality is that every story has two ways of being told, and this one is no exception.
A bend in the river
Despite not being a very well known work internationally, it is written by the Nobel Prize for Literature VS Naipaul.
The darker side of marriage is the central theme of Gone girl, a psychological thriller that has become one of the best-known and most popular books in recent times.
Salmon's song by Toni Morrison is another of Obama's recommendations, and which tells the story of a man's family, who takes steps of success in business, trying to hide his origins to integrate into white society.
Mailer's heroes are the main protagonists of this novel that will not leave you indifferent And as Obama has done, we also highly recommend that you buy it and above all that you enjoy it.
The underground railway It is not just any book and it is that in the Colson Whitehead, which won the US National Book Award for Narrative with this book, tells in great detail what slavery was like in the XNUMXth century. The protagonist of this book is Cora, a young woman who will make your heart tremble and that she is a slave along with her mother on a plantation, where they both work and from where her mother decides to flee, leaving her in the greatest of solitudes.
Creative stagnation and writing problems are the most common problems for writers. It is precisely about this problem that Dorsi Lessing speaks in The golden notebook, where Anna Wulf, a novelist suffers from this problem.
Are you still wondering whether to follow Barack Obama's recommendation?
To close this list, the former president of the United States recommends that we read Gilead, which is the title of the novel, but also of a small town in Iowa where not everything is what it seems and there is a parallel story that will surely hook you and catch you.
How many and which of the works recommended by Barack Obama have you already read and which ones are you planning to read in the near future?. Tell us in the space reserved for comments on this entry, in our forum or through any of the social networks in which we are present.
I do not know if Trump will read those books but if he keeps most of his promises (and if they let him) he will become the best president in the history of the United States regardless of who he may.
