Recent Posts How to apply RFID and other IoT technologies in theme parks?
RFID tags sense chemicals and gases in the environment
The laboratory integrates sensor functions into RFID tags, and has developed an RFID tag that works in the ultra-high frequency (UHF) band, which can measure glucose concentration and forward the information. In the future, the team plans to use the RFID tag to sense chemicals and gases in the environment, such as carbon monoxide.
However, Kantareddy believes that this specific response antenna has a weakness, which is multipath interference. That is, what the reader receives is not only the direct response signal from the RFID tag, but also the multipath signal that the direct response signal reaches the reader through environmental reflection.
Bhattacharyya emphasized that the new solution also solves a major problem faced by antenna-based RFID sensing technology-mutual interference when a large number of RFID tags are simultaneously launched. Users who were previously confused by the signals from a large number of short-range passive tags can now place the reader far away, and the reader will only sound an alarm when a certain substance does appear in the environment.
In the demonstration experiment, the research team demonstrated an RFID glucose sensor based on a commercially available glucose sensor. When glucose touches the tag, the electrolyte in the sensor reacts chemically to generate electricity and provide additional energy to the RFID.
Kantareddy said that as soon as the user receives a signal in the semi-active mode, they know that the tag has found glucose. The user can further determine the glucose content based on the duration of the semi-active mode.
In addition, the new RFID detector is more efficient, because on the one hand, when the target substance is not sensed, the RFID tag works in a passive mode and does not consume power; on the other hand, the target substance in the environment is touching the detector. Time also produces energy, so the process of sending signals does not consume much battery.
