At the retrospective level, RFID technology electronic tags can be affixed to fresh food, and relevant data of the fresh product can be obtained through big data to help customers view historical information and ensure food safety. From the perspective of work flow, RFID technology has the hope to improve the accuracy of inventory to avoid extravagant waste of food materials.
What are the advantages of RFID warehouse management system?
The existence of the above warehouse problems has had an adverse impact on the development and operation of the enterprise, and it is necessary to urgently solve and improve the warehouse management level. The emergence of RFID warehouse management system provides enterprises with a more convenient, efficient and intelligent warehouse management mode.
At the same time, through the UHF RFID tag binding to the goods, it can accurately distinguish the actual management problems such as batch, model, product name, warehousing time, supplier, status, etc., and the management and control is more in line with modern management needs.
The receipt data does not need to be recorded manually, and the system automatically collects and counts to ensure the accuracy of the receipt data.
The system will automatically optimize the picking walking path, no need to walk back and forth, just one walk to finish picking goods.
One of its most important advantages is non-contact identification. It can work in harsh and harsh environments, and it can and has strong penetrating power, and can quickly identify and read tags.
The data capacity of the RFID tag is very huge, it can be expanded to 10k according to the needs of users, which is much higher than the capacity of 2,725 digits in the two-dimensional code bar.
It can be operated dynamically, its tag data can be dynamically modified by programming, and it can be dynamically tracked and monitored, as long as the object attached to the RFID tag appears within the effective recognition range of the reader.
Long service life. Because of its strong anti-interference, RFID tags are not easy to be destroyed and have a long service life.
Anti-collision, within the effective recognition range of the reader, it can read multiple RFID tags at the same time.
High security. RFID tags can be attached to the product in any form, and the tag data can be encrypted with passwords to improve security.
As soon as the RFID tag enters the effective recognition range of the reader, it will immediately start to read the data. Under normal circumstances, the recognition can be completed in less than 100 milliseconds.
Of course, every technology has its pros and cons. The development of RFID technology to this day will also have its shortcomings, that is, the technical application of UHF frequency band is not wide enough, the technology is not mature enough, the related products are expensive, and the stability is not high.
