In China, visiting relatives and friends, and visiting for entertainment are indispensable with wine culture. With the improvement of people’s living standards, the requirements for wine quality are constantly changing.
The so-called old wine is wine that has been stored for a long time, such as Moutai more than ten years ago. With the “consumption upgrade” of liquor, old wine has become more and more recognized by consumers, and the concept of “old wine = good wine” has gradually become popular.
Consumer recognition and the growth of the market scale not only benefit the “old wine” category, but also bring certain challenges to the old wine market. One of the biggest challenges is how to enable consumers to buy real old wine with confidence.
As the most recognized liquor/old wine brand, there are already many “tutorials” on the Internet to assist consumers in identifying the authenticity of old wines, such as looking at the details of the bottle, sealing rubber cap, and anti-counterfeiting. Manuals and other external methods, but this method of external identification by the naked eye will inevitably have a time of “eye punching”, so the identification by technical means is particularly important.
To put it simply, the anti-counterfeiting traceability system means that each bottle of Moutai has its own unique “ID card”, which records the basic information of the bottle of Moutai, such as year, origin, etc., which can be identified by scanning codes and RFID chips. Way to authenticate the old wine.
The new version of the stickers is more difficult to copy, which increases the cost of counterfeiting. In terms of logistics, “See Zhen System” has also created an exclusive WMS+ logistics warehouse distribution management system, and every process of all Moutai liquor circulation is clearer.
