Geotab has already provided a set of technical solutions that can track the usage and location information of vehicles. Now, after adding the NFC read-write module, the fleet management company can judge whether the driver is driving safely (for example, information such as vehicle speed) and calculate the work based on the read information.
The core device of the solution is the GeotabGO6 device, which consists of a wireless communication module, GPS and computing modules, etc., and is connected to the car’s OBDII port. Combined with sensors, the device can provide information such as the vehicle’s position, speed, tire pressure, seat belts, sudden braking, sharp turns, sharp acceleration, and overtime usage.
After installing the NFC reader/writer, the first thing a driver enters into the car is to bring his NFC key close to the reading and writing device to read data. The NFC reader reads the ID code of the tag, if the ID has been authorized (the NFC code of the key is associated with a specific driver, and this information is stored in the G06 software system), the green light of the G06 device is on, and the key can be inserted into the hole , start the car.
This solution not only makes it easier for managers to know where the vehicle is driving, but also whether the driver is driving efficiently and safely. Through this solution, fleet managers can determine which drivers need to improve their driving skills, thereby reducing the incidence of fleet accidents and unnecessary costs, and improving the efficiency of the fleet.
