3 Reliability testing of electronic label packaging Through bubble inspection, X-ray inspection, dynamic balance uniformity inspection and durability test, the tires with RFID electronic tags are tested to verify the flexural pressure, anti-interference and high temperature resistance of the electronic tags and whether it will affect the tire performance.
With the help of dynamic balance uniformity testing equipment, we test tires implanted with RFID electronic tags. The results show that the actual mass of the RFID electronic tag is only 0.02g, and the tire’s dynamic balance uniformity will not be affected after being implanted in the tire.
The best implantation position and implantation method of the electronic tag are verified through experiments, and the reliability test of the electronic tag is mainly researched, mainly through the air bubble, X-ray, dynamic balance uniformity, durability test and testing of the test tire. Tests and other tests are carried out, and the test results show that the implantation of RFID tags in the tires will not affect the quality and safety performance of the tires.
From the positioning principle, it can be divided into three types: RSSI ranging, TOF ranging, and TDOA ranging. The three methods correspond to different precisions.
WIFI positioning adopts the principle of RSSI positioning, so the accuracy is relatively low. The construction of WIFI network is not for special purpose and positioning services.
That is to say, as long as your mobile phone terminal has Wi-Fi turned on, it will have one or repeated frame listening and response with the AP in the space in the background. These can be frame listening, which will reveal your approximate position in the space.
Secondly, the workload of WIFI positioning is relatively large for the location map. WIFI positioning is to obtain relative coordinates, that is, the coordinates of the mobile phone relative to the WIFI base station or AP.
The second advantage of WIFI positioning is that the cost is low. The chip module of WIFI is already around 10 yuan, and the price of WIFI base station and AP is less than 100 yuan, and it can perform data transmission and positioning functions, so it can meet the needs of low-cost large-scale need for expansion.
In terms of positioning accuracy, the Bluetooth positioning algorithm has no advantages compared with WIFI, so the accuracy is related to the density of the Bluetooth beacon, and the accuracy is about 1-5 meters. Bluetooth positioning advantages:
The obvious advantage of Bluetooth positioning is that the power consumption is relatively low, and the power consumption of Bluetooth is lower than that of WIFI. If a dedicated positioning network is deployed For the reliability of the system, it is more robust and stable than the WIFI network that takes into account data transmission and positioning.
According to the delay from the active RFID tag sending the signal to the reader reading the tag information to assist in judging the location information of the tag, the longer the delay, the farther, and vice versa. The relatively new technology also uses the TDOA algorithm, which is generally used in RFID in the UHF frequency band, but it is rarely used and the cost is very high.
RFID base station equipment is relatively abundant, and there are many high-power equipment and low-power card readers, which are suitable for networking in various occasions.
The same accuracy requirements need to be met. Compared with UWB positioning, the deployment of RFID base stations or readers is relatively complex and the number is large.
The UWB positioning algorithm is based on three-point positioning. If the number of base stations is reduced, it will greatly affect the positioning accuracy.
